cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "tdfpy: A Python package for parsing and centroiding Bruker timsTOF mass spectrometry data"
abstract: >-
  tdfpy is a Python package for reading Bruker timsTOF data from analysis.tdf
  and analysis.tdf_bin files inside a .d directory. It accesses the SQLite
  metadata and compressed binary peak data directly, so workflows do not need
  the Bruker native library. High-level readers represent data-dependent
  acquisition, data-independent acquisition, and parallel reaction monitoring
  runs through frames, precursors, isolation windows, targets, and transitions.
  Metadata is loaded when a run is opened, while raw peak arrays are decoded
  only when requested. Spectrum extraction can retain ion mobility as arrays of
  mass-to-charge ratio, intensity, and inverse reduced mobility. Processing
  pipelines support region exclusion, smoothing, configurable noise filters,
  and two centroiding approaches: greedy peak merging in floating-point mass
  space and watershed region growth in time-of-flight index space. Frames and
  acquisition objects can also be selected by identifiers, mass-to-charge
  ranges, and retention time. tdfpy is intended for proteomics workflows that
  need scriptable access to timsTOF measurements, mobility-resolved peaks, and
  PASEF acquisition metadata on Linux, macOS, or Windows.
